# API Design Rules - Greek ERP/CRM System

## Core API Standards

- **REST Convention**: Standard HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)
- **Base URL**: `/api/v{version}/` with proper versioning (e.g., `/api/v1/business-entities`)
- **Status Codes**: Use standard HTTP status codes consistently
- **Content Type**: `application/json` for all requests and responses
- **Character Encoding**: UTF-8 to support Greek characters
- **Response Format**: Consistent JSON structure with success/error fields

## Versioning Strategy

- **URL Versioning**: Include version in URL path (`/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`)
- **Backwards Compatibility**: Support previous versions for critical integrations
- **Deprecation**: Clear deprecation timeline and migration path
- **Version Validation**: Validate and enforce supported API versions

## Request/Response Standards

- **Pagination**: Cursor-based pagination for large datasets
- **Filtering**: Query parameters for filtering Greek business data
- **Sorting**: Multiple sort fields with Greek collation support
- **Search**: Full-text search with Greek character support
- **Metadata**: Include pagination and response metadata

## Greek Business API Patterns

- **AFM Validation**: Endpoints for Greek tax number validation
- **DOY Lookup**: Tax office information and validation endpoints
- **AADE Integration**: MyDATA submission and status tracking
- **VAT Calculation**: Location-aware Greek VAT rate calculation
- **Greek Addressing**: Proper Greek address formatting and validation

## Error Handling Standards

- **Consistent Format**: Standardized error response structure
- **Error Codes**: Business-specific error codes (AUTH_001, VAL_002, etc.)
- **Greek Messages**: Error messages in both Greek and English
- **Field Validation**: Field-specific validation error details
- **Status Mapping**: Appropriate HTTP status codes for different error types

## Authentication & Authorization

- **JWT Requirements**: Include company context in all tokens
- **Permission Checks**: Endpoint-level permission validation
- **Company Isolation**: Enforce multi-tenant boundaries
- **Rate Limiting**: Protect sensitive endpoints from abuse
- **Audit Integration**: Log all API access and modifications

## Greek Compliance Endpoints

- **AADE Submission**: Invoice submission to Greek tax authority
- **VAT Calculation**: Dynamic Greek VAT rate calculation
- **Tax Reports**: Greek compliance reporting endpoints
- **Business Validation**: AFM, DOY, and Greek phone validation
- **Compliance Status**: Real-time compliance status checking

## Performance & Caching

- **Response Caching**: Cache frequently accessed reference data
- **Company-Specific Keys**: Cache keys with company isolation
- **Cache Invalidation**: Proper cache invalidation on data changes
- **Rate Limiting**: Protect against abuse with configurable limits
- **Response Times**: <200ms for simple operations, <2s for complex

## Documentation Standards

- **OpenAPI Specification**: Complete API documentation with examples
- **Greek Examples**: Sample requests/responses with Greek business data
- **Error Documentation**: All possible error codes and responses
- **Authentication**: Clear authentication and authorization requirements
- **Versioning**: Document version differences and migration guides

## Monitoring & Health Checks

- **Health Endpoints**: System health and component status
- **Metrics Collection**: API usage, performance, and error rates
- **Greek Integration**: Monitor AADE connectivity and submission rates
- **Alerting**: Automated alerts for system issues and failures
- **Audit Trails**: Complete request/response logging for compliance

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never expose internal error details in production responses
- ❌ Don't skip input validation for Greek characters and business data
- ❌ Never return data from other companies (company isolation breach)
- ❌ Don't hardcode Greek business rules in API logic
- ❌ Never skip rate limiting on sensitive endpoints
- ❌ Don't ignore proper HTTP status codes
- ❌ Never expose sensitive data (AFM, personal info) in logs
- ❌ Don't skip API versioning for breaking changes
- ❌ Never allow SQL injection through query parameters
- ❌ Don't skip caching for frequently accessed reference data

